# Independent Method Claim

**Claim 1.** A method for operating a mobile phone as a hearing aid remote controller, the method comprising:

detecting, by the mobile phone, insertion of a Secure Digital (SD) card into an SD card slot of the mobile phone, wherein the SD card comprises a radio frequency interface configured to communicate wirelessly with a hearing aid device;

in response to detecting the insertion of the SD card, initializing, by the mobile phone, a driver application configured to establish a communication interface between the mobile phone and the SD card radio frequency interface;

establishing, via the initialized driver application, a wireless communication link between the SD card radio frequency interface and a wireless transceiver of the hearing aid device;

transmitting, from the mobile phone to the hearing aid device via the established wireless communication link, an identifier request requesting a unique device identifier associated with the hearing aid device;

receiving, at the mobile phone, a response to the identifier request, the response comprising the unique device identifier of the hearing aid device;

transmitting, from the mobile phone to a remote server via a network connection, an authentication request comprising the unique device identifier and a user credential associated with the mobile phone;

receiving, at the mobile phone from the remote server, an authentication confirmation indicating that the hearing aid device and the mobile phone are authorized to communicate with one another;

in response to receiving the authentication confirmation, enabling, on the mobile phone, a remote control user interface configured to receive user input for adjusting one or more operational parameters of the hearing aid device; and

transmitting, from the mobile phone to the hearing aid device via the wireless communication link, one or more control commands corresponding to the user input received via the remote control user interface, wherein the one or more control commands cause the hearing aid device to adjust the one or more operational parameters accordingly.
